## Highlights
1. MOF morphology, crystalline structure alteration and "quasi-MOF" construction affect photocatalytic performance.
2. Efficient photocatalytic one-pot hydrogenation and N-alkylation of nitrobenzenes and benzonitriles.
3. N-alkylation of benzonitriles with alcohols was achieved firstly in heteroegeneous catalysis.
4. Reaction mechanism was proposed with the assistance of in situ DRIFTS.
